# DNS Code Block Rules

The “One-Minute Fix” DNS record is the core utility of the site.
Every DNS example MUST appear inside a reusable `CodeBlock` component with a copy button.

This applies to:
- SPF records
- DKIM selectors
- DMARC policies
- Any DNS TXT record examples

---

# 1) Required component

Create and reuse a component:

components/ui/CodeBlock.tsx

Requirements:

- Monospace font
- Dark background
- Horizontal scroll on mobile
- Copy-to-clipboard button
- Visual feedback after copy ("Copied!")

---

# 2) UX behavior

The component must include:

• Copy button (top-right corner)  
• Clipboard API  
• Button text changes to "Copied!" for ~2 seconds  
• Accessible for keyboard users  

Example behavior:

User clicks "Copy"  
↓  
DNS record copied  
↓  
Button changes to "Copied!"

---

# 3) Visual design

The code block must include:

- rounded-lg
- dark neutral background
- monospace font
- padding
- horizontal scroll for long records

Example style:

- bg-neutral-900
- text-neutral-100
- font-mono
- text-sm
- overflow-x-auto

---

# 4) Placement rules

The CodeBlock must appear:

• inside the "One-Minute Fix" section  
• near the top of the page  
• above long explanations  

This ensures fast triage for:

- founders
- IT admins

---

# 5) Example usage

Example DNS record block:

v=spf1 include:_spf.google.com ~all

